---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Font Finder — Developer-First Typography Tools"
  description="Learn about Font Finder's mission to make font identification transparent, privacy-first, and completely free using open-source Google Fonts."
>
  <article class="py-12 sm:py-20 px-4 sm:px-6 max-w-[1000px] mx-auto">
    <div class="mb-10">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
        <div class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#e4f222]"></div>
        <span class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-[#8a8f98]">MISSION STATEMENT</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-[510] text-[#ffffff] tracking-[-0.022em]">
        About Font Finder
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] sm:text-[16px] text-[#8a8f98] leading-relaxed font-normal">
        Building a cleaner, faster, and more honest way to discover and use open-source web typography.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-[#8a8f98]">
      
      <section class="rounded-[12px] border border-[#23252a] bg-[#0f1011] p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-sm">
        <div class="border-l-2 border-[#e4f222] pl-3.5 mb-3">
          <h2 class="text-[16px] sm:text-[17px] font-[510] text-[#ffffff] tracking-[-0.012em]">
            The Problem with Legacy Font Finders
          </h2>
        </div>
        <p class="text-[#d0d6e0]">
          Legacy font tools force users through aggressive popup ads, mandatory email signups, paywalled matches, and suggestions for commercial fonts costing hundreds of dollars.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[#d0d6e0]">
          Font Finder operates on a simple principle: when you see typography you love, you need the name, verified open-source Google Fonts alternatives, and copy-ready CSS declarations in seconds.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="rounded-[12px] border border-[#23252a] bg-[#0f1011] p-5 sm:p-6 shadow-sm">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#e4f222]"></span>
            <h3 class="font-[510] text-[15px] text-[#ffffff]">100% Free & Unlimited</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="text-[13px] text-[#8a8f98]">No scan limits, no account creation, and zero paywalls.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-[12px] border border-[#23252a] bg-[#0f1011] p-5 sm:p-6 shadow-sm">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#e4f222]"></span>
            <h3 class="font-[510] text-[15px] text-[#ffffff]">Verified Google Fonts</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="text-[13px] text-[#8a8f98]">Every match links to official Google Fonts repositories under the SIL Open Font License.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-[12px] border border-[#23252a] bg-[#0f1011] p-5 sm:p-6 shadow-sm">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#e4f222]"></span>
            <h3 class="font-[510] text-[15px] text-[#ffffff]">Zero Image Retention</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="text-[13px] text-[#8a8f98]">Canvas pixel analysis runs strictly in-memory within your browser tab.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-[12px] border border-[#23252a] bg-[#0f1011] p-5 sm:p-6 shadow-sm">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#e4f222]"></span>
            <h3 class="font-[510] text-[15px] text-[#ffffff]">Production CSS Blueprints</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="text-[13px] text-[#8a8f98]">Tested <code class="font-mono text-[12px] text-[#d0d6e0] bg-[#161718] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded-[4px] border border-[#23252a]">@import</code> and <code class="font-mono text-[12px] text-[#d0d6e0] bg-[#161718] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded-[4px] border border-[#23252a]">font-family</code> declarations with live specimen testing.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
